GPL-3.0 COMPONENT — tools/imsg-dump/
================================================================================

`tools/imsg-dump/` is NOT covered by the MIT license above. It is licensed
under GPL-3.0 and carries its own LICENSE file in that directory.

WHY IT EXISTS

It links the GPL-licensed `imessage-database` crate to parse Apple's
`attributedBody` typedstream format. That parser is not optional: since macOS
Big Sur, much of a message's text is not stored in the `text` column at all,
and readers that only query that column silently return empty strings for
large portions of modern message history. Getting this wrong produces a system
that appears to work while missing much of its corpus.

WHY THE BOUNDARY IS SHAPED THIS WAY

`imsg-dump` is invoked strictly as a SUBPROCESS. It is never linked, imported,
or otherwise combined into the Python code under `src/`. Communication is via
process invocation and structured output on stdout.

That process boundary is deliberate and load-bearing: it is what allows the
core to remain MIT-licensed while the GPL parser does the typedstream work.

IF YOU CHANGE HOW IT IS INVOKED

Vendoring `imsg-dump` into the core, linking the `imessage-database` crate
directly, or otherwise combining the two beyond a process boundary changes the
licensing analysis. That is yours to reason about — the arrangement here was
chosen specifically to avoid that question, and it only holds while the
boundary does.

